<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Definitely what I was trying to convey. I see a couple possible fixes for this:</p>
<ul>
<li>Go with the original plan, which was to [DATA EXPUNGED]. I feel like that's a cop out, so unless there's some kind of consensus here that it'd be an improvement, I'm reluctant to use it.</li>
<li>Simply change the line to state that the brightness was not in fact so severe, so they're unsure as to how the personnel were blinded. Not sure how to word this, at the moment.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<blockquote>
<p>Even if that is what you're going for, there's nothing in the rest of the SCP that thematically matches with that ability, so it reads just like random unrelated junk to make this more spooooooky.</p>
</blockquote>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Spoopy is what I was really hoping to avoid. I simply wanted to leave a blank space to add some mystery. It made sense to me that this would be something that can/should not be perceived. The whole thing is centered around rebirth, so I hope that part doesn't seem off. Between the behavior of the -1s vs -2s:</p>
<p>(-1s: Violent and gluttonous. Seek to gratify their own needs at the expense of others.)<br />
(-2s Show compassion, have sense of community are willing to sacrifice to benefit another. Ready to 'pass on')</p>
<p>The human tissue bit, the d-class's dialogue, the birth ending, the physical appearance of the -1s/-2s, the conversion of a -1 into a -2&#8230; it all should add up to make it clear that what was 'witnessed' was a kind of (as you quite aptly put it) 'majesty cognitohazard' as the instance passes over.</p>
<p>I'm almost certain that part fits with the rest of the skip, but is there anything I could do to make it clearer? I wanted to avoid the blatant &quot;The -1s/-2s DNA matches deceased individuals.&quot; or somesuch. All ears.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I would rather have been left in complete mystery then given what was said in the last addendum.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This has mainly been about the 'flash of light' bit. I'm not sure if you're still referring to that here, or if by 'last addendum' you mean the kicker at the end? If it's the latter, I think I'll have to leave it as-is. Most people enjoyed that bit.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
